  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 140 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nFriday night through Thursday:\n\nThe next best chances for storms in a very uncertain pattern\ncomes on Friday night into Saturday morning. 13.12z guidance\nshows a 500mb trough ejecting northeastward out of Colorado and\npropagating northeast to eastward into Saturday morning with the\nvort max going right through southern WI. In the lower levels, a\nsurface low currently over Kansas is expected to follow a\nsimilar track into southern Wisconsin with a strong push of\n925-850mb moisture transport out ahead of it. Guidance suggests\nrain moving into southwest Wisconsin after 7pm Friday night with\nthe most widespread rain coming in after midnight through\ndaybreak Saturday. Forecast soundings show fairly warm air aloft\nwith minimal instability to work on. Therefore, am thinking the\nsevere potential is fairly low on this round of storms and will\nmoreso be another beneficial rainfall. Can't rule out some\nlightning for the late evening Friday and Saturday morning for\nany events and farmers markets occuring over this timeframe.\n\nSunday is rather questionable at the moment for whether there\nwill be any rain as the 13.12z NAM/GFS both push the boundary\nout of southern Wisconsin in the wake of the Saturday low while\nthe ECMWF is slower to bring it through. Have some small chance\nPOPs in there to cover the ECMWF solution.\n\nBeyond that, the early portion of next week features a broad\nridge of high pressure before return southerly flow kicks back\nin. Another trough looks to swing down from Canada around mid-\nweek which could lead to the next chances for rain/storms.\n\n\nHalbach",
